From 4d3076c53ead4982cd460d8bac6c4a24c1c77bb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 23:51:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 16/24] Wake-up synthetic message becomes a directive
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The bare "." we used in patch 0024 satisfied the API ("final message
must be a user message") but produced bad model behavior: when the
wake-up turn ran, the model saw the dot, treated it as a no-op
continuation, and replied with generic text from prior context
("Still waiting on the Bazel expert to finish...") — ignoring the
<system-reminder> from patch 0017 listing the ready task_ids.

Replace the dot with explicit directive text that mirrors the
system-reminder:

  [Background task complete] Call read_task_result(task_id="...")
  for the task_id listed in the <system-reminder> above to fetch
  the result, then respond to the user with what you learned. Do
  not say you are still waiting — the task has finished.

The synthetic flag still suppresses the chat-UI render
(UserMessage at routes/session/index.tsx:1261 filters !synthetic)
and the per-step user-message wrap in prompt.ts. So the directive
is visible to the model API but invisible in the user's chat.

The "do not say you are still waiting" sentence directly counters
the observed failure mode.
---
 packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts | 36 ++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts b/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts
index 281711c..b037d21 100644
--- a/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts
+++ b/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts
@@ -1321,18 +1321,30 @@ NOTE: At any point in time through this workflow you should feel free to ask the
       )(function* (sessionID: SessionID) {
         return yield* prompt({
           sessionID,
-          // Hivemind: non-empty placeholder. Empty text gets dropped in
-          // MessageV2.toModelMessagesEffect (parts collapse to length 0
-          // for empty-text user messages), leaving the previous assistant
-          // message as the trailing message in the model API messages
-          // list — which Claude rejects as "assistant message prefill".
-          // A single dot is the smallest non-whitespace content that
-          // survives every downstream filter; the synthetic flag still
-          // suppresses the per-step user-message wrap and the chat-UI
-          // rendering, so the model just sees a one-character user turn
-          // and the system-reminder injection from patch 0017 drives
-          // actual behavior on this turn.
-          parts: [{ type: "text", text: ".", synthetic: true }],
+          // Hivemind: directive synthetic user message. Earlier we used
+          // "." as a minimal non-empty placeholder so the API call
+          // wouldn't be rejected as "assistant message prefill", but
+          // the model treated the dot as a no-op and replied with
+          // generic continuation text ("Still waiting on the Bazel
+          // expert to finish..."). The system-reminder block injected
+          // alongside (see "Background tasks ready" in this file)
+          // wasn't enough on its own — the user-turn text needs to
+          // mirror the directive so the model can't miss it.
+          //
+          // The synthetic flag still suppresses the per-step
+          // user-message wrap and the chat-UI render, so this text
+          // is invisible to the user but visible to the model API.
+          parts: [
+            {
+              type: "text",
+              synthetic: true,
+              text:
+                "[Background task complete] " +
+                'Call read_task_result(task_id="...") for the task_id listed in the ' +
+                "<system-reminder> above to fetch the result, then respond to the user " +
+                "with what you learned. Do not say you are still waiting — the task has finished.",
+            },
+          ],
         })
       })

